  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1: Possible record highs today.\n\nExpect plenty of sunshine with northern fringe of 5h ridge\nacross the Carolinas and westerly flow to send temps 15 to 20\ndegrees above normal this afternoon with records attainable at\nleast for our Piedmont/Roanoke locations. See climate section\nbelow.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Frontal boundary with shower/storm chances\ntonight-Thursday mainly across WV and the Alleghanys.\n\nWest-east front backdoors in tonight, with some upper support\nacross WV/Shenandoah Valley pushing across early Thursday. A\nmodel consensus points to a tighter gradient of where measurable\nshowers occur versus the have nots. Areas along the I-64\ncorridor and maybe as far south as Bluefield to Roanoke will see\nshower chances tonight-Thursday, with some potential\nthunderstorm development Thursday afternoon in the mountains.\nAreas from southside VA into NC from the mountains to Piedmont\nstay fairly dry.\n\nKey Message 3: Stronger front Friday brings blustery winds and\ncooler temps into the weekend.\n\nA strong front and decent 5h trough arrive Friday. Coverage of\nshowers will be greatest in the mountains then a typical jump to\nthe Piedmont and points east later in the afternoon/evening with\nthis type of system. \n\nThe big story will be the winds and the colder temps to follow\nheading into the weekend.\n\nModels are showing impressive 6 hr pressure rises of 8-12 mb\nright behind the front late Friday afternoon into Fri night with\n8h jet 45-50 kts. Forecast soundings and the pattern look for\nfavor some potential wind advisory headlines for that time\nperiod along our Blue Ridge and adjacent areas. For now will\nmention in the Hazardous Weather Outlook.\n\nTemperatures go from 10 to 20 degrees above normal, to 10 to 15\ndegrees below normal in the course of 24 hrs Friday into\nSaturday. Still looks reasonable that freezing temperatures will\noccur Sat night in the mountains and with winds weakening frost\nstill looks like a good bet into the Piedmont.\n\nThe surface high should linger into early next week but return\nflow should allow temps to be getting back closer to normal\nMonday-Tuesday.",
